        {
          "id": "ai-safety-security-quality-q2",
          "number": 2,
          "marks": [
            "decides"
          ],
          "text": "How do you make LLM-as-judge trustworthy?",
          "points": [
            "A judge is <strong>a model you must evaluate</strong>: label ~100 cases by hand, measure agreement (% / Cohen's kappa)",
            "Narrow rubric: <strong>one criterion per call</strong>, binary or 1–3 scale, with the reason before the score",
            "Known biases: <strong>position, verbosity, self-preference</strong> → swap order, length-control, use a different model family",
            "Give it <strong>references</strong>: the source passages, the expected answer, the tool result",
            "Re-check agreement when the judge <strong>model or rubric changes</strong>; keep humans on a sample",
            "<svg class=\"md-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"1.15em\" height=\"1.15em\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"vertical-align:-0.2em;flex-shrink:0\"><path d=\"m22.61 18.99-9.08-9.08c.93-2.34.45-5.1-1.44-7C9.79.61 6.21.4 3.66 2.26L7.5 6.11 6.08 7.52 2.25 3.69C.39 6.23.6 9.82 2.9 12.11c1.86 1.86 4.57 2.35 6.89 1.48l9.11 9.11c.39.39 1.02.39 1.41 0l2.3-2.3c.4-.38.4-1.01 0-1.41m-3 1.6-9.46-9.46c-.61.45-1.29.72-2 .82-1.36.2-2.79-.21-3.83-1.25C3.37 9.76 2.93 8.5 3 7.26l3.09 3.09 4.24-4.24-3.09-3.09c1.24-.07 2.49.37 3.44 1.31 1.08 1.08 1.49 2.57 1.24 3.96-.12.71-.42 1.37-.88 1.96l9.45 9.45z\"></path></svg> <strong>ResoDesk:</strong> planned: RAG faithfulness + citation judge and a conversation judge (right tool, read-back done), calibrated on hand labels (C-12)"
          ],
          "links": [
            {
              "label": "LLM as a Judge",
              "target": "05-LLM-Production/10-Evaluation/03-LLM-as-a-Judge"
            },
            {
              "label": "LLM as judge for trajectories",
              "target": "03-Agentic-AI/09-Evaluation &amp; Observability/04-LLM-as-judge for trajectories"
            }
