        {
          "id": "ai-safety-security-quality-q6",
          "number": 6,
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Safety, security and quality — what's the difference?",
          "points": [
            "<strong>Quality:</strong> is it right and useful? → evals, judges, monitoring",
            "<strong>Safety:</strong> does the system cause harm by its own behaviour? → policy, guardrails, refusals, handoff",
            "<strong>Security:</strong> can an attacker make it do harm? → injection, data exfiltration, excessive agency, abuse of cost",
            "They overlap: a hallucinated dose is quality <strong>and</strong> safety; a leaked record is security <strong>and</strong> safety",
            "Map to a standard: <strong>OWASP Top 10 for LLM Apps 2025</strong> for security, a harm policy for safety, an eval suite for quality",
