    {
      "id": "ai-safety-security-quality-c",
      "letter": "C",
      "name": "Security: injection, tools and agents",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "ai-safety-security-quality-q7",
          "number": 7,
          "marks": [
            "decides"
          ],
          "text": "What is prompt injection — direct vs indirect — and how do you defend against it?",
          "points": [
            "Instructions and data share <strong>one channel</strong>, so text can act as an instruction",
            "<strong>Direct:</strong> the user types it. <strong>Indirect:</strong> it arrives in content the model reads (docs, web, email, tool output, images, memory)",
            "No prompt-level fix: delimiters and classifiers <strong>lower frequency, not possibility</strong>",
            "Contain the blast radius: <strong>least-privilege tools, rules decide, confirmation, no free outbound channel</strong>",
            "Test it: an <strong>injection eval set</strong> across every input channel, asserting no unauthorised action",
